# Schema migration policy

`20261008_01_schema_baseline` is an adoption baseline for both empty databases and existing installations that do not yet have Alembic revision tracking. Existing tables are left in place; existing account IDs and password hashes are retained, existing `students.department` text and attendance rows are preserved, and department associations are added as nullable foreign keys. Legacy `admin`, `faculty`, and `student` role strings are normalized in place to canonical role names.

Before applying a migration to an institution's database, make an operator-managed, restorable backup. Apply with `flask --app app db upgrade`. Production application startup does not create or modify schema. Do not use `flask db stamp` to bypass the adoption migration. Future schema changes must be authored as revisions and applied through the same command.

The initial adoption revision is intentionally irreversible because dropping its additions would discard department associations and changing a baseline underneath live data is unsafe.
